iki/Lost_River","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/0315bad20a9f57ef.png","depthRange":["550 - 1000 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Limestone Outcrop","Sandstone Outcrop","Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":["Disease Research Facility","Gargantuan Fossil","Ghost Forest Arch Cache","Lost River Laboratory"]},{"name":"Mountains Caves","link":"/wiki/Mountains_Caves","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/2ab3bb1af8cccbe8.png","depthRange":["0 - 380 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":["Thermal Vents (2)"]},{"name":"Mushroom Forest Caves","link":"/wiki/Mushroom_Forest_Caves","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/0196abce16a01707.png","depthRange":["170 - 250 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Safe Shallows Caves","link":"/wiki/Safe_Shallows_Caves","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/f341271a8d4dc104.png","depthRange":["10 - 75 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Limestone Outcrop","Sandstone Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Sea Treader's Tunnel Caves","link":"/wiki/Sea_Treader%27s_Tunnel_Caves","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/ebb0b44dcaf7a7ed.png","depthRange":["200 - 340 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Limestone Outcrop","Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Underwater Islands Caves","link":"/wiki/Underwater_Islands_Caves","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/b8309487c34a152f.png","depthRange":["205 - 255 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Crash Zone Mesas","link":"/wiki/Crash_Zone_Mesas","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/70fe010fb6811e5e.png","depthRange":["150 - 330 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Limestone Outcrop","Sandstone Outcrop","Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Lava Geyser","link":"/wiki/Lava_Geyser","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/6b3dd2facbfe1363.png","depthRange":["60 - 560 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Varies"],"pointsOfInterest":[]},{"name":"Lava Castle","link":"/wiki/Lava_Castle","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/0462731a8c612ec7.png","depthRange":["1100 - 1300 meters"],"pointsOfInterest":["Alien Thermal Plant"],"harvestingNodes":[]},{"name":"Inactive Lava Zone Corridor","link":"/wiki/Inactive_Lava_Zone_Corridor","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/abcaa6edfb086aa4.png","depthRange":["800 - 1200 meters"],"harvestingNodes":["Shale Outcrop"],"pointsOfInterest":[]}],"articles":[{"name":"Wrecks","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/7e6e897a213dd8d5.png","summary":"The Wrecks are explorable pieces of debris from the Aurora. They have a wide range of sizes. Large Wrecks contain valuable technology in the form of Fragments and sometimes Data Boxes or Supply Crates, while Small Wrecks contain only a limited amount of fragments.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Wrecks","coords":null,"poiType":null},{"name":"Lifepod 5","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/671ab3db5669ef06.png","summary":"The Standard 2-Berth Emergency Lifepod 5 is the vessel in which Ryley Robinson survived the crash of the Aurora at the beginning of Subnautica, landing in the Safe Shallows.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Lifepod_5","coords":null,"poiType":null},{"name":"Destroyed Lifepods","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/b77cac3ac0300aa5.png","summary":"Destroyed Lifepods are small survival vessels that were launched from the Aurora during its descent. While several lifepods survived initially, by the time the player wakes after being unconscious for three hours in Lifepod 5, it is the only one still intact, the others having sunk or been attacked.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Destroyed_Lifepods","coords":null,"poiType":null},{"name":"Degasi Seabases","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/befa0000935ba433.png","summary":"The Degasi Seabases are habitats constructed by the three survivors from the Degasi, a spacecraft that crashed on Planet 4546B about a decade before the Aurora. There are three such bases found within the game world, two of which have several sub-bases in their surroundings. All of the bases are in various states of disrepair.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Degasi_Seabases","coords":[{"x":"-800","y":"80","z":"-1055"},{"x":"-760","y":"15","z":"-1115"},{"x":"-705","y":"80","z":"-1165"}],"poiType":null},{"name":"Aurora","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/fa7177771fcfaaa0.png","summary":"The Aurora is a spacecraft sent to the Ariadne Arm by the Alterra Corporation to build a phasegate. However, its secondary mission, unknown to most of the crew, was to search for and possibly rescue the survivors of the Degasi crew.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Aurora","coords":null,"poiType":null},{"name":"Quarantine Enforcement Platform","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/7db9bd0cfd42cec4.png","summary":"The Quarantine Enforcement Platform is a massive Alien weapon system that is located on the Mountain Island. It is the source of the energy beam responsible for causing both the Degasi and Aurora to crash on Planet 4546B, as well as destroying the Sunbeam during its rescue attempt.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Quarantine_Enforcement_Platform","coords":[{"x":"375","y":"8","z":"1106"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Disease Research Facility","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/d93b3e53f3732398.png","summary":"The Disease Research Facility is a destroyed Alien Base located in a cave that can be accessed from the Lost River Junction and the Mountains Corridor. Built around one thousand years ago, sometime before the imprisonment of the Sea Emperor Leviathan, the main purpose of this Disease Research Facility was to infect creatures with the Kharaa Bacterium to study their reaction to the disease. The sole specimen that survived the Kharaa Bacterium was sent to the Primary Containment Facility for further testing in order to synthesize a cure for the bacterium.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Disease_Research_Facility","coords":[{"x":"-252","y":"-814","z":"316"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Alien Thermal Plant","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/0e82fce246bf2084.png","summary":"Thexa0Alien Thermal Plant is the smallest of the four main Alien Bases. It can be found in the Inactive Lava Zone, within the Lava Castle. It was built around one thousand years ago.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Alien_Thermal_Plant","coords":[{"x":"-75","y":"-1182","z":"5"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Primary Containment Facility","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/2a1733f7fb035f18.png","summary":"The Primary Containment Facility, also known as the Emperor Containment Facility, Sea Emperor Prison or merely the Prison, is an Alien Base located within the Lava Lakes that serves as the final major story location. It was built by the Precursor Race around one thousand years ago and is home to the last remaining Sea Emperor Leviathan, along with the five remaining Sea Emperor Leviathan Eggs. There are two entrances to the Lava Lakes containing the Primary Containment Facility; co-ordinates are -300 -1270 -150 and 90 -1240 360, southeast, and directly north of the Lava Castle, respectively.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Primary_Containment_Facility","coords":[{"x":"200","y":"-1440","z":"-222"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Alien Arch Caches","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/2d19bd3c3e552964.png","summary":"These chambers contain Alien Arches and are scattered throughout the world, located in the Northwestern Mushroom Forest, the Crag Field, the Ghost Forest, the Floating Island, the Mountain Island, and the Bulb Zone. Each of these Alien Arch Caches is linked to the Primary Containment Facility, for the purpose of getting the ingredients for Hatching Enzymes, with the exception of the Floating Island Arch Cache, which is linked to the Mountain Island Arch cache.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Alien_Arch_Caches","coords":[{"x":"1383","y":"-296","z":"757"},{"x":"-81","y":"-290","z":"-1360"},{"x":"-662","y":"2","z":"-1050"},{"x":"-931","y":"-611","z":"991"},{"x":"340","y":"61","z":"903"},{"x":"-803","y":"-227","z":"409"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Sanctuary Caches","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/773fb449982f7752.png","summary":"Threexa0Alien Cachesxa0serving as sanctuariesxa0can be found located in a cave in the Deep Sparse Reef, right next to the Sea Treader's Path Wreck (Wreck 7), deep within a cave in the Northern Blood Kelp Zone, and inside an impact crater left behind by a meteor in the Dunes. These threexa0Caches each require one Purple Tablet toxa0access.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Sanctuary_Caches","coords":[{"x":"-880","y":"-305","z":"-790"},{"x":"-554","y":"-534","z":"1521"},{"x":"-1187","y":"-378","z":"1130"}],"poiType":"alienBases"},{"name":"Lost River Laboratory Cache","image":"/images/subnautica/wikia/dd17a5c2a8c10761.png","summary":"The Laboratory Cache is found in thexa0Ghost Canyon of the Lost River. It was set up to study the Ancient Skeleton and several other specimens within the Lost River. This Cache is unique in that it requires the Orange Tablet found in the Deep Grand Reef Degasi Base to unlock.","type":"article","link":"http://subnautica.wikia.com/wiki/Lost_River_Laboratory_Cache","coords":[{"x":"-1111","y":"-685","z":"-655"}],"poiType":"alienBases"}],"wrecks":[{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":-1201,"y":-324,"z":-396}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":929,"y":-198,"z":593}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":1309,"y":-215,"z":570}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":-1448,"y":-332,"z":723}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":-1632,"y":-334,"z":83}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":-1210,"y":-217,"z":7}},{"title":"Large Wreck","type":"largeWrecks","coords":{"x":-290,"y":-222,"